Exit Status - Part2
We already know how to capture the command exit status. However
when we are making our own scripts then being an author we need to provide our own exit status to the system.
This is a very good practice to understand if the script is completed successfully or not.


# script.sh
echo Hello World
exit # to come out myown use exit 1 other commands wont execute
echo Final World

# Output
bash script.sh
echo $?


# script.sh
echo Hello World
exit 1
echo Final World

# Output
bash script.sh
echo $?

